# tally 2.2.1 P41, the fix review's F5 and n3: a for domain's where over a window-dated decision is the window's hole per
# tuple, never REFCORE-NOT-YET (review g1fix n3a fr_where, lf_where sm_where). Before W8: REFCORE-NOT-YET.
=== lf_where.tally
model n3
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-10
  start 2026-03-01
  end 2026-06-30
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index qs = 1..2
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place konto2: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input w: date
input w3: date
input dy_day: date
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  w = window(2026-04-29, 2026-05-02) "s"
  w3 = window(2026-04-10, 2026-04-12) "s"
  dy_day = 2026-06-05 "s"
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"
  opening[konto2] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-03-01 start "s"
move dx: transfers
  on w
  reads konto
  leg cash from world to konto amount if bal(konto) > 0 PLN then amt else amt
ask sm_where: q for q in qs where sum(m.cash.amount for m in transfers over 2026-04 .. 2026-05) > 0 PLN
ask plain: bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
=== expect plain sm_where
plain: 500.00 PLN
  cut 2026-06-10
sm_where (q = 1): ?"date within window(2026-04-29, 2026-05-02) not precise enough for a binding over dx" (w)
sm_where (q = 2): ?"date within window(2026-04-29, 2026-05-02) not precise enough for a binding over dx" (w)
warning: WARN-UNREAD input dy_day is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input w3 is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD place konto2 is read by nothing
